<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Setup and smoothing estimates</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For a positive-definite matrix <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{q,M}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{X\sim P,\,Y\sim Q}\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert_{M}^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\,,\qquad\lVert x\rVert_{M}\coloneqq(x^{\mathsf{T}}Mx)^{1/2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></mrow></munder><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>q</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>M</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">≔</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>𝖳</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{q,M}(P,Q)\coloneqq\inf_{X\sim P,\,Y\sim Q}\bigl(\mathbb{E}\lVert X-Y\rVert_{M}^{q}\bigr)^{1/q}\,,\qquad\lVert x\rVert_{M}\coloneqq(x^{\mathsf{T}}Mx)^{1/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Recall that</p>
<table id="S4.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p)\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathsf{N}(0,I)(\mathrm{d}p)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∗</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖭</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}\coloneqq\pi*\mathsf{N}(0,\eta I)\,,\qquad\Pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x\,\mathrm{d}p)\coloneqq\pi_{\eta}(\mathrm{d}x)\,\mathsf{N}(0,I)(\mathrm{d}p)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\mid Y=y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\mid Y=y</annotation></semantics></math> be drawn from <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Recalling the definition (<a href="#S2.E1" title="Equation 2.1 ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>) of the proximal operator, throughout this section we write</p>
<table id="S4.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>prox</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{y}^{+}\coloneqq\operatorname{prox}_{\eta V}(y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">It is easy to check the identities</p>
<table id="S4.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}\,(y-\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y])\,,\qquad\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-2}\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}\,(y-\mathbb{E}[X\mid Y=y])\,,\qquad\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)=\eta^{-1}I-\eta^{-2}\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>⩽</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\eta\leqslant 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\kappa+\eta}\,I\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq\frac{1}{1+\eta}\,I\preceq I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\kappa+\eta}\,I\preceq\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}\preceq\frac{1}{1+\eta}\,I\preceq I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The RGO potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta^{-1})\,I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta^{-1})\,I</annotation></semantics></math>. The
Brascamp–Lieb covariance inequality <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>κ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\preceq(\kappa^{-1}+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">For the reverse bound, the
Cramér–Rao inequality (see, e.g., <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>, Theorem 3.5.8]</cite>) gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{Cov}(X\mid Y=y)\succeq(1+\eta^{-1})^{-1}I\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Substitute both bounds in
(<a href="#S4.E1" title="Equation 4.1 ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following is the key estimate that decomposes the stochastic gradient error into a bias term and a stochastic error term.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.2</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Stochastic gradient estimates)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Write</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)\coloneqq g_{\eta}(y)+b_{\eta}(y)+\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\,,\qquad\mathbb{E}\xi_{\eta}(y;G)=0\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then, for all <math id="S4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,y,y^{\prime},G,G^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert b_{\eta}(y)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\eta^{3/2}\sqrt{d}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}e^{\langle u,\xi_{\eta}(y;G)\rangle}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant e^{\eta\,\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y^{\prime};G)\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.170em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E5"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lVert\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)-\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G^{\prime})\rVert</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>G</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant\sqrt{\eta}\,\lVert G-G^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Proximal optimality gives
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})=(y-x_{y}^{+})/\eta</annotation></semantics></math>. Define</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{y}(u)\coloneqq V(x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}u)-V(x_{y}^{+})-\sqrt{\eta}\,\langle\nabla V(x_{y}^{+}),u\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo>⪯</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\preceq\nabla^{2}\rho_{y}\preceq\eta I</annotation></semantics></math>, and under <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{\eta,y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>R</mi><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{\eta,y}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(X-x_{y}^{+})/\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> has density
proportional to <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>u</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>u</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\mapsto e^{-\lVert u\rVert^{2}/2-\rho_{y}(u)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Call this law <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We have</span></p>
<table id="S4.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{2}(\mathsf{r}_{y},\mathsf{N}(0,I))\leqslant\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}[\lVert\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\rVert^{2}]}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\lVert U\rVert^{2}}\leqslant\eta\sqrt{d}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, the first inequality combines Talagrand’s inequality for the standard
Gaussian with the Gaussian log-Sobolev inequality; the second uses that
<math id="S4.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}(0)=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\rho_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz; and the last
follows by integration by parts since <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-strongly
log-concave with its mode at <math id="S4.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\,,\qquad\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\nabla\rho_{y}(G)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>U</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\eta}(y)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{r}_{y}}\nabla\rho_{y}(U)\,,\qquad\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;G)=\nabla V(x_{y}^{+})+\eta^{-1/2}\,\nabla\rho_{y}(G)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">The gradient of <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>η</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, so
(<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 4.6 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a>) gives (<a href="#S4.E2" title="Equation 4.2 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>). Since <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>g</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{g}_{\eta}(y;\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, the standard Gaussian concentration inequality
gives (<a href="#S4.E3" title="Equation 4.3 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>), and the same observation gives
(<a href="#S4.E5" title="Equation 4.5 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>). Finally, <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\mapsto x_{y}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\mapsto x_{y}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math> is non-expansive and
<math id="S4.SS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla V</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="S4.SS1.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>-Lipschitz, proving (<a href="#S4.E4" title="Equation 4.4 ‣ Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We will also need high-order regularity of the smoothed potential. The key
point is a near-Gaussian cancellation, which is stronger than the generic moment bound for a
strongly log-concave law. The Gaussian cumulant estimates used in the proof
are collected in <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.3</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Derivatives of the smoothed potential)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For every integer <math id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 2</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S4.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E7.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\sqrt{d}\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S4.E8"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.059em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>v</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>v</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{y\in\mathbb{R}^{d},\,\lVert v\rVert=1}\,\lVert D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)[v,\cdot^{k-1}]\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E8.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.170em">!</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leqslant(k-1)!\,\eta^{-(k-2)/2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="S4.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E9.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lVert\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)-\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y^{\prime})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>HS</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.085em">∥</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.085em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lVert\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y)-\nabla^{2}V_{\eta}(y^{\prime})\rVert_{\mathrm{HS}}\leqslant 2\eta^{-1/2}\,\lVert y-y^{\prime}\rVert\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the normalized RGO from the proof of
<a href="#S4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma 4.2 (Stochastic gradient estimates). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. Its potential has Hessian between
<math id="S4.SS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>I</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1+\eta)I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)I</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{y}</annotation></semantics></math> be the optimal transport
from the standard Gaussian to <math id="S4.SS1.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{r}_{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝗋</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{r}_{y}</annotation></semantics></math>. Caffarelli’s contraction theorem
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>, applied in both directions, gives</span></p>
<table id="S4.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>η</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>I</mi><mo>⪯</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>⪯</mo><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="1.889em">,</mo><msub><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.1389em">∥</mo></mrow><mi>op</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.1389em">⩽</mo><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.170em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1+\eta)^{-1/2}I\preceq DT_{y}\preceq I\,,\qquad\lVert DT_{y}-I\rVert_{\mathrm{op}}\leqslant\eta/2\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4.10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">almost everywhere.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">By (<a href="#A3.E22" title="Equation C.22 ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.22</span></a>), for <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\geqslant 3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⩾</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\geqslant 3</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mi>k</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Cum</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{k}V_{\eta}(y)=-\eta^{-k}\operatorname{Cum}_{k}(X\mid Y=y)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Under the RGO,
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msqrt><mi>η</mi></msqrt><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>T</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X=x_{y}^{+}+\sqrt{\eta}\,T_{y}(G)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>𝖭</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\sim\mathsf{N}(0,I)</annotation></semantics></math>. Translation invariance and homogeneity of
cumulants, followed by (<a href="#S4.E10" title="Equation 4.10 ‣ Proof. ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.10</span></a>) and
<a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6 (Cumulants of a near-identity Gaussian image). ‣ C.2 Cumulants and derivatives of smoothed potentials ‣ Appendix C Gaussian analysis ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a> with <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo>⩽</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{T}\leqslant\eta/2</annotation></semantics></math>, prove
(<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 4.7 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>)–(<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>).
The case <math id="S4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=2</annotation></semantics></math> is <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma 4.1 (Hessian bounds for the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>; integrating the
<math id="S4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=3</annotation></semantics></math> estimate (<a href="#S4.E8" title="Equation 4.8 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.8</span></a>) along a segment gives
(<a href="#S4.E9" title="Equation 4.9 ‣ Lemma 4.3 (Derivatives of the smoothed potential). ‣ 4.1 Setup and smoothing estimates ‣ 4 Proof of the 𝑊_2 guarantee ‣ Smoothed Picard Hamiltonian Monte Carlo" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>).
